.TH PEKIT.LOCK 5 2026-10-28 "Peios pekit 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
pekit.lock \- the libraries a pekit workspace pins, and where they come from
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I WORKSPACE/pekit.lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I pekit.lock
is a JSON file at the root of a
.BR pekit (1)
workspace.
It pins each library the workspace imports, and each library those import, at a commit of the git repository it comes from, so that every checkout of the workspace builds with the same libraries.
.B pekit lock
writes it.
Every other command reads it as it is written.
.PP
The file is one object with two arrays,
.B sources
and
.BR libraries .
Either can be left out, and is then empty.
.B pekit lock
writes both, the libraries sorted by path, with two spaces of indentation.
.SS sources
Each source says where the libraries under a prefix of import paths come from.
A library comes from the first source whose
.B prefix
is its path, or a part of its path that ends before a
.BR / .
A source has these fields:
.TP
.B prefix
A prefix of import paths, such as
.BR github.com/gcslib .
.TP
.B git
The git repository, a URL or a path, as
.BR git (1)
reads it.
.TP
.B dir
The directory in the repository that holds the libraries under the prefix: the library
.IB PREFIX / REST
is the directory
.IB DIR / REST
of the repository.
Empty or left out for the repository's root.
.TP
.B rev
The revision the source follows: a branch, a tag, or a commit.
.B HEAD
if left out.
.PP
A library that no source covers takes a source by the convention of Go's modules:
its path's first three parts,
.IB HOST / OWNER / REPO\fR,
are the prefix, the repository is
.BI https:// HOST / OWNER / REPO\fR,
the directory is the repository's root, and the revision is
.BR HEAD .
.B pekit lock
adds the source to the file, where it can be edited.
.SS libraries
Each pinned library has these fields, all of which
.B pekit lock
writes:
.TP
.B path
The library's import path, such as
.BR github.com/gcslib/gcc .
.TP
.B git
The repository it was pinned from.
.TP
.B dir
Its directory in the repository, empty for the repository's root.
.TP
.B commit
The commit it is pinned at, its whole name of 40 hexadecimal digits.
.TP
.B tree
The SHA-256 digest of the library's directory as it was exported, as pekit's store names a tree, in 64 hexadecimal digits.
A library in
.I .gcsl/libraries/
whose tree has another digest differs from its pin.
.SH BEHAVIOR
.B pekit lock
finds every library the workspace imports, and pins each that the file does not pin, at the commit its source's revision names.
With
.BR \-\-update ,
it pins every library again.
It exports each library it pins, with
.BR "git archive" ,
into
.IR .gcsl/libraries/PATH/ ,
and drops each pinned library that nothing imports, with its directory.
.PP
.BR build ,
.BR test ,
.BR run ,
.BR query ,
.BR package ,
and
.B publish
put back each pinned library missing from
.IR .gcsl/libraries/ ,
from the commit it is pinned at, and warn of each one there that differs from its pin.
A build with
.B \-\-strict
fails if the workspace has no
.IR pekit.lock ,
if a library it imports is not pinned, if a pinned library differs from its pin, or if
.B GCSL_LIBRARY_PATH
is set.
.PP
Repositories are kept as bare clones in the cache directory's
.IR git/ ,
and fetched only to resolve a revision or to get a commit they do not have.
A workspace whose libraries are pinned and fetched builds without the network.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I WORKSPACE/pekit.lock
This file.
Commit it.
.TP
.I WORKSPACE/.gcsl/libraries/
The pinned libraries, exported.
Do not commit it.
.TP
.I CACHE/git/
Bare clones of the libraries' repositories.
.SH EXAMPLES
This lock pins the gcc library from its own repository, and takes the ppk library from a directory of another repository's
.B main
branch:
.PP
.in +4n
.EX
{
  "sources": [
    {
      "prefix": "github.com/gcslib/gcc",
      "git": "https://github.com/gcslib/gcc",
      "dir": "",
      "rev": "HEAD"
    },
    {
      "prefix": "github.com/gcslib/ppk",
      "git": "/srv/git/pekit",
      "dir": "gcslib/github.com/gcslib/ppk",
      "rev": "main"
    }
  ],
  "libraries": [
    {
      "path": "github.com/gcslib/gcc",
      "git": "https://github.com/gcslib/gcc",
      "dir": "",
      "commit": "72dae8c75eabc34c63615380a9197e1021a39952",
      "tree": "9134e446ef194af0f256bff0b3c5f6cb134fe40012d40510861ebf3a43588019"
    }
  ]
}
.EE
.in
.PP
The lock does not pin the ppk library, so
.B pekit lock
pins it from the second source.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR pekit (1)
.PP
https://learn.peios.org/pekit
